-- title:
--   Surjectivity of n-th powers U^{(k)}→ U^{(k+e)} in a complete DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`, and assume $R$ is adically complete with respect to $\mathfrak m$. Let $n$ be a natural number with $0 < n$, and let $e$ be a natural number such that the ideal generated by the image of $n$ in $R$ equals $\mathfrak m^{e}$, i.e. $\operatorname{span}\{(n : R)\} = \mathfrak m^{e}$. Let $k$ be a natural number with $e < k$, and let $w \in R^{\times}$ lie in `principalUnits R (k + e)`, that is, $w - 1 \in \mathfrak m^{k+e}$ (here `principalUnits R j` is the subgroup of units $u$ with $u - 1 \in \mathfrak m^{j}$). Then there exists a unit $u$ of $R$ with $u - 1 \in \mathfrak m^{k}$, i.e. $u \in$ `principalUnits R k`, such that $u^{n} = w$ in $R^{\times}$. Thus raising to the $n$-th power maps the $k$-th principal unit group onto the $(k+e)$-th one under the stated hypotheses.
--
--   This is the standard statement that in a complete discrete valuation ring the $n$-th power map carries the higher unit group $U^{(k)}$ onto $U^{(k+e)}$ whenever $v(n) = e$ and $k > e$ (a convenient, non-sharp threshold covering both the tame case $e = 0$, where it is Hensel's lemma, and the wild case). It is used in the computation of the index of the subgroup of $n$-th powers in the unit group of a local field, and thence in local index computations for $p$-adic fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_exists_mem_principalUnits_pow_eq.lean

